        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_988280775.1",
        "comments": "The assembly ddCarPrat1.hap1.1 is based on 53x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species looks to work as a functional tetraploid, except for one set of chromosomes, where it looks to have only two copies on the HiC map. Based on this, the species contains a total number of 30 chromosomes and looks to be aneuploid. The HAP1 file contains 2 chromosome-level curated haplotypes and the other two scaffold-level haplotypes are in HAP2 file.",
